{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n#define MOD 1000000007\n#define N 33\ntypedef long long ll;\nll n, m, bin[66];\nstruct mat {\n    ll v[N][N];\n    mat() { memset(v, 0, sizeof(v)); }\n    mat operator*(const mat &r) const {\n        mat res;\n        for (int i = 0; i <= m; ++i)\n            for (int j = 0; j <= m; ++j)\n                for (int k = 0; k <= m; ++k)\n                    res.v[i][j] = (res.v[i][j] + v[i][k] * r.v[k][j]) % MOD;\n        return res;\n    }\n} ans, P[66][N], S[66][N], A[66][N];\nll read() {\n    ll x = 0, f = 1;\n    char ch = getchar();\n    while (ch < '0' || ch > '9') { if (ch == '-') f = -1; ch = getchar(); }\n    while (ch >= '0' && ch <= '9') { x = x * 10 + ch - '0'; ch = getchar(); }\n    return x * f;\n}\nsigned main() {\n    n = read(); m = read();\n    int len = 0;\n    ll tmp = n;\n    while (tmp) { bin[len++] = tmp % m; tmp /= m; }\n    if (len == 0) len = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i <= m; ++i) ans.v[0][i] = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < len; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j <= m; ++j) A[i][0].v[j][j] = 1;\n        if (i == 0) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < m; ++j) {\n                A[i][j].v[m][m] = 1;\n                for (int k = 0; k < m; ++k) {\n                    if (k != j) { A[i][j].v[k][k] = 1; continue; }\n                    for (int l = 0; l <= m; ++l) A[i][j].v[k][l] = 1;\n                }\n            }\n        } else {\n            for (int j = 0; j < m; ++j) {\n                if (j == 0) A[i][j] = S[i-1][0];\n                else A[i][j] = S[i-1][j] * P[i-1][j-1];\n            }\n        }\n        P[i][0] = A[i][0];\n        for (int j = 1; j < m; ++j) P[i][j] = P[i][j-1] * A[i][j];\n        S[i][m-1] = A[i][m-1];\n        for (int j = m-2; j >= 0; --j) S[i][j] = A[i][j] * S[i][j+1];\n    }\n    int pos = 0;\n    for (int i = len-1; i >= 0; --i) {\n        ll cnt = bin[i];\n        while (cnt--) {\n            ans = ans * A[i][pos];\n            pos = (pos + 1) % m;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << ans.v[0][m] << endl;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef mat_mul(A, B, mod):\n    n = len(A)\n    C = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        for k in range(n):\n            if A[i][k]:\n                aik = A[i][k]\n                for j in range(n):\n                    C[i][j] = (C[i][j] + aik * B[k][j]) % mod\n    return C\n\ndef identity(n):\n    return [[1 if i == j else 0 for j in range(n)] for i in range(n)]\n\ndef zero(n):\n    return [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\ndef main():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n    \n    # base-m digits (least significant first)\n    bin_digits = []\n    tmp = n\n    while tmp:\n        bin_digits.append(tmp % m)\n        tmp //= m\n    if not bin_digits:\n        bin_digits = [0]\n    length = len(bin_digits)\n    \n    size = m + 1  # matrix dimension\n    \n    # Initialize ans as a row vector (first row all ones)\n    ans = zero(size)\n    for j in range(size):\n        ans[0][j] = 1\n    \n    # A, P, S are lists of lists of matrices\n    A = [[None for _ in range(m)] for _ in range(length)]\n    P = [[None for _ in range(m)] for _ in range(length)]\n    S = [[None for _ in range(m)] for _ in range(length)]\n    \n    for i in range(length):\n        # Build A[i][j] for j = 0..m-1\n        if i == 0:\n            for j in range(m):\n                mat = zero(size)\n                # last row: only (m,m) = 1\n                mat[m][m] = 1\n                for k in range(m):\n                    if k != j:\n                        mat[k][k] = 1\n                    else:\n                        for l in range(size):\n                            mat[k][l] = 1\n                A[i][j] = mat\n        else:\n            for j in range(m):\n                if j == 0:\n                    A[i][j] = S[i-1][0]\n                else:\n                    A[i][j] = mat_mul(S[i-1][j], P[i-1][j-1], MOD)\n        \n        # Compute prefix products P[i][j]\n        P[i][0] = A[i][0]\n        for j in range(1, m):\n            P[i][j] = mat_mul(P[i][j-1], A[i][j], MOD)\n        \n        # Compute suffix products S[i][j]\n        S[i][m-1] = A[i][m-1]\n        for j in range(m-2, -1, -1):\n            S[i][j] = mat_mul(A[i][j], S[i][j+1], MOD)\n    \n    pos = 0\n    for i in range(length-1, -1, -1):\n        cnt = bin_digits[i]\n        while cnt:\n            ans = mat_mul(ans, A[i][pos], MOD)\n            pos = (pos + 1) % m\n            cnt -= 1\n    \n    print(ans[0][m])\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.05931779369711876, -0.023571161553263664, -4.017272294731811e-05, 0.0, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -0.0002696150622796267, -0.3166050910949707, -9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, -3.814689989667386e-06, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -0.005244426429271698, -0